  "verified_against": {
    "source": "release-manifest.json",
    "agrees": true,
    "note": "Hashes were downloaded from the published v5.27.0 release assets and hashed independently. v5.27.0 reconverts the teaching voice: what limits it is now an obligation its prompt carries, not a shorter toolbox. It used to declare read, write, edit, skill and ask -- no bash, no grep, no glob -- so the voice whose whole purpose is to explain the code could not search it, and its body forbade it from checking what it had just written four lines after telling it to write it. It now declares the same reach as the orchestrator and every MCP server the release ships, and two rules replace the old prohibition: work out loud or not at all, and close the loop you open. The difference is in kind, not degree -- working in silence is not a tool a permission can deny, so that discipline can only live in the prompt. Third-party credentials (GDE & MVP) and one person's editor and terminal (LazyVim, Tmux, Zellij) were removed from the persona: this content ships rebranded to a public-sector institution, and neither belonged in it. The character itself is unchanged. In DARQ the voice installs as arquitecto-darq, as it already did. Only the `pegasus` artifact changed; install.sh and the two builder scripts are byte-identical to v5.25.1, so DARQ's own installer does not change in this re-pin either."
  }
